    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d777">

                <pb facs="0861" n="851" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg851"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11–548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-06T13:00:00-05:00">November 6, 1948—1
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4327. French Emb has already taken up with Dept questions mentioned in ur 5746
                    Nov 5, 5 p. m. Dept did not give any definite answers in respect courses of
                    action such contingencies. For ur info Dept has not yet received from Nanking
                    its report discussion there but Emb has now been instructed supply account of
                    meeting and its views.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d777-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d777-f1" n="5" xml:id="d777-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 1558, November 6, 1 p. m., to the Ambassador in China, not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
